[Music]  welcome back to cbs this morning it's  been a very tough week on capitol hill  where four police officers caught up in  the mob violence on january 6th  testified in very graphic detail about  what they experienced  pictures still get to you that includes  capitol police officer harry dunn  who talked with nicole killian about the  impact of the attack on him  and his family and what he wants to see  from the congressional investigation  nicole good morning my heart broke  listening to all the officers but  harry dunn in particular really got to  me how's he doing  well gail officer dunn told me that he  felt  every range of emotion when he testified  from  anger to hope and he says that since his  appearance on capitol hill this week  he's received an  outpouring of support but also attacks  especially  on social media you swear i affirmed  you heard four stories four stories from  january 6.  there were hundreds and hundreds and  hundreds of more stories  that need to be and could be there could  be a need to be told  u.s capitol police officer harry dunn  says he's been getting disparaging  messages  ever since his testimony before the  house select committee  investigating january 6th so many people  were so proud of you were so proud of  you and  then here come the naysayers and the  negative nazis and  people are saying i've been bought and  paid off and  how much did you sell out for you are a  coward you're a traitor  you're not an amer you're not a real  police officer and then that just kind  of  took me to a  low place he hasn't gotten any death  threats like metropolitan police officer  mike fanon  who received one while he was testifying  i wish they would have killed all you  scumbags  what do you make of that message so i  had to talk to him about it because i  it makes me so upset but the 13-year  veteran of the force said it's  no worse than when rioters hurled racial  slurs at him during the capital attack  it was almost just as hurtful like  because i pride myself on my credibility  my integrity and my honor like i'm not  getting  anything out of this it has been an  isolating experience for dunn  who often works six days a week while  also  juggling therapy it's lonely doing this  thing that's why me and mike have  i believe such a strong relationship we  have the same  goal in mind and that's about  accountability and justice  and the truth even at the highest levels  there was an attack carried out on  january 6  and a hit man sent them who were you  talking about  there was a rally prior to the attack  it was a rally those facts exist  um there were quotes said like we got to  fight like hell  or you won't have a country left are you  talking about the former president those  were his words  do you think the former president should  testify  that's their that's their job i don't  know perhaps the hardest testimony dunn  has to give  is to his own nine-year-old daughter  what have you told her about all of this  uh you got to try to you know shield  your kids  from his uh but you also want to be  honest with them  and um i literally just say some bad  people  try to do some bad things to the capitol  and to the country  and uh the good guys won so  i mean how is she processing it i can  tell that uh  she hugs me a little tighter um she has  me a little longer  and uh god i love those hugs  you know they're amazing so i don't i  oblige  her as long as she wants officer  dunn's daughter was not at the hearing  but some of his family was he says he is  optimistic about  the select committee and would be  willing to testify again  even if republicans break out and launch  their own  investigation he also hasn't given up on  an independent 9 11 style panel anything  to get to the root causes of what  happened nicole thank you so much  and that was great reporting i don't  know how anybody could look at that  video  whether you're a republican or a  democrat and not  want to hear or understand the relevance  of those  officers who were there that day and  harry harry dunn's daughter's hugs make  up for a lot but he should not have to  go he went through enough on january 6.  he should not have to go through what  people are doing today all of them did  and then you see the  the voicemail that michael fanon got the  fact that these guys are getting any  kind of criticism after they risk their  lives  to save the people that are now  criticizing them it's just mind-boggling  to me i  applaud them all for speaking up the way  that they under the worst circumstances  they were protecting  the capital they were protecting the  congress and they were protecting  the constitution and harry done alluded  to it there is still a lot of officers  off the job that we don't hear about yes  that are still suffering that day and  he's right officer done accountability  justice  and the truth is what everybody those  are just four of the stories  exactly right

